          <div class="about-text">
            <h2>A Foundation in Compassionate Care</h2>
            <p>
              Dr. Hany Soliman graduated in 1994 from Cairo University Veterinary School. He spent over a decade practicing veterinary medicine abroad before moving to the United States in 2005. To further his education and obtain his veterinary license in the U.S., he attended Oklahoma State University for three years. Upon completing his certifications, he chose to bring his expertise to the great state of California.
            </p>
            
            <h2>The Transition to In-Home Euthanasia</h2>
            <p>
              For many years, Dr. Soliman worked as an associate veterinarian at Banfield and various private clinics. During his time in traditional clinic settings, he noticed a recurring, heartfelt request from pet owners: families frequently asked for at-home options to say their final goodbyes.
            </p>
            <p>
              Recognizing that the clinical environment with its strange smells, bright lights, and unfamiliar noises could cause unnecessary stress for a sick or elderly pet, Dr. Soliman felt called to make a change. He left private practice with a singular mission: to provide families with a peaceful, compassionate alternative. 
            </p>
            <p>
              By offering in-home pet euthanasia, Dr. Soliman allows beloved companions to gently pass away in the comfort of their own homes, surrounded by love and familiar comforts. His ultimate goal has always been to give pet owners the warmth, patience, and deep understanding they truly need during such a heartbreaking time.
            </p>
            
